    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0033" n="543" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg543"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1–1648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Macatee</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-01-16T18:00:00+02:00">January 16, 1948—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. Emile Ghory of AHE, just returned from Cairo meeting with Mufti, informed
                    official ConGen following:</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>General national administration for whole Palestine will be established by
                        Arabs on day British terminate mandate. Administration now being organized
                        on basis Cairo press communique 5 January.</item>
                    <pb facs="0034" n="544" xml:id="pg544"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Believes Abdullah<anchor n="1" xml:id="d8-f1"/> regardless private
                        thoughts must accept Palestine Arab administration although admits
                        possibility various parts Palestine may be annexed to bordering states. The
                        line is that unimportant who takes over Palestine provided Palestine remains
                        Arab. Preference is for unified Palestine state.</item>
                </list>
                <p>[Here follow Mr. Ghory’s further thoughts, including the observations that Arab
                    attacks on Jewish settlements were “for demonstration, training and probing
                    purposes” and that “Arms arriving increasing rate and young Arabs undergoing
                    rigid training.”]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Macatee</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
